From 8e544d4e6dfa8b403503997cbbb8dce7e54de5ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Catalin Niculescu <cn.cata@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 20:56:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] cpu_guard: step the fan up while the CPU is above a
 threshold
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Engages at --high (95 °C), adds --step every --step-every seconds while the
smoothed package temperature is above --target (92 °C), steps back down below
target - cool-margin, then restores the starting speed and releases the pad.
Meant to be started detached (systemd-run --user) by other tools during heavy
jobs; no sudo needed once the udev rule is installed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
